DXMT v0.80 (on top of the other dxmt-*-v0.80.patch files): upstream commit
ab984cf (3Shain/dxmt, 2026-04-27, not in v0.80), backported unchanged.
A tessellation/geometry (mesh) pipeline that rasterizes with no pixel shader
gets no colour attachments; Metal otherwise aborts the process with
"Mesh Render Pipeline Descriptor Validation fragmentFunction must not be nil"
(Advanced Warfare, after the first campaign cutscene).
Siliconium ships it for Advanced Warfare only (payload/steam/aw-d3d11.dll).

commit ab984cfd0083651ba0f8b1e66e348c4be99a02d6
Author: Feifan He <feifan@codeweavers.com>
Date:   Mon Apr 27 13:50:45 2026 +0800

    fix(d3d11): disable color attachments in mesh pipeline if no pixel shader is bound and rasterization is enabled
    
    Metal has been inconsistent here because the same setup is fine on ordinary render pipeline but triggers assertion for mesh render pipeline. FB22625154.
    
    Signed-off-by: Feifan He <feifan@codeweavers.com>

